{"uid":"kernel/ed25519.c","name":"ed25519.c","qualname":"kernel/ed25519.c","kind":"module","file":"kernel/ed25519.c","line":1,"end_line":888,"language":"c","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"","description":"","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["kernel/ed25519.c::ed_u64","kernel/ed25519.c::ed_fe","kernel/ed25519.c::ed_ge","kernel/ed25519.c::ed_sha512_init","kernel/ed25519.c::ed_sha512_update","kernel/ed25519.c::ed_sha512_final","kernel/ed25519.c::ed25519_verify"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
{"uid":"kernel/ed25519.c::ed_u64","name":"ed_u64","qualname":"ed_u64","kind":"type_alias","file":"kernel/ed25519.c","line":23,"end_line":23,"language":"c","signature":"typedef unsigned long long ed_u64;","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Docstring: kernel/ed25519.c -- Ed25519 signature verification.","description":"Freestanding verify-only half of Ed25519 (RFC 8032): SHA-512 plus\ntwisted-Edwards verification over Curve25519. No signing, no key\ngeneration; private scalars never exist in the kernel. The file\nincludes nothing and uses only unsigned char, unsigned long and\nunsigned long long, so the same source builds for the kernel\n(-ffreestanding) and for the host suite (tests/test_sign.c).\n\nField elements are four little-endian 64-bit limbs. Products use\n__uint128_t schoolbook multiply with repeated 38-folds, and\nscalars reduce mod L by binary long division, so no\ntranscription-risk prime multiple tables are needed. Point decoding\nrecovers x by exponentiation with a sqrt(-1) adjustment computed at\nrun time, so the only transcribed constants are the base point\nencoding, L, q and the SHA-512 table, all generated by script and\npinned by tests/test_sign.c.\n\nEvery input to verification is public (signature, message, key),\nso variable-time field arithmetic is acceptable here; the scalar\nmultiply still uses double-and-add-always out of hygiene.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"kernel/ed25519.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
